# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aff Exteriors — environment configuration
#
# The app runs out of the box with NO configuration using a local browser-based
# data store (great for development and demos). When you are ready to connect a
# real Firebase backend, copy this file to ".env.local" and fill in the values
# from your Firebase project's web app config (Project settings > General >
# Your apps > SDK setup and configuration).
#
# As soon as all VITE_FIREBASE_* values below are present, the app automatically
# switches from the local store to real Firebase (Google sign-in + Firestore +
# Storage). Note: a user can sign in with Google but only becomes a "team
# member" once an admin creates their users/{uid} role document.
#
# Full step-by-step instructions are in FIREBASE_SETUP.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
